! The `ph.x` input that generated `reference.out.ph-alas-raman`:
!
!   pw.x -in alas-raman.in && ph.x -in alas-raman.ph.in
!
! `PHonon/examples/example05`'s response input, on the ground state of
! `alas-raman.in`. It prints the electro-optic tensor (`el_opt.f90`, dε/dE in
! Rydberg a.u.) and the Raman tensor (`raman_mat.f90`, dε/dτ in inverse bohr),
! which are the two quantities P35 computes.
!
! **The committed output of this run is evidence, not a reference.** The vendored
! ph.x 7.5 does not reproduce QE's own committed example05 (generated with v6.0):
! -1.8681 against -0.78497 for the Raman tensor and 157.87 against 40.4578 for the
! electro-optic one, and its own internal check -- the "dielectric constant from
! finite-differences" that dhdrhopsi prints beside the analytic one -- gives -0.288
! against 8.8143 where v6.0 has 8.8116 against 8.8147. Tightening eth_rps and
! eth_ns by four orders moves it by 1e-2. Nothing in the test suite compares
! against the numbers in this file; P35 is validated against a finite difference
! of the dielectric tensor instead, and this output is kept so that the claim
! about ph.x can be checked without a Fortran build. The pseudopotentials
! committed here are a different distribution of the same two (their MD5s differ
! from the ones example05 downloads), which is not the explanation: eps agrees to
! 4e-4 between the runs, and the check that fails is internal to a single run.
phonons of AlAs at Gamma
 &inputph
  tr2_ph=1.0d-12,
  prefix='alas',
  epsil=.true.,
  trans=.true.,
  lraman=.true.,
  elop=.true.,
  zeu=.true.,
  amass(1)=26.98,
  amass(2)=74.92,
  fildyn='alas.dynG',
 /
0.0 0.0 0.0
